  "final_message": "The bug was in `collect` in `billing/payments.py`. When a customer had no default payment method, it returned `None` without calling `record_failure`. So the invoice stayed open, no retry was scheduled, no `invoice.payment_failed` event fired, and the subscription never moved to `past_due`.\n\nThe fix is that `collect` now calls `record_failure(ctx, invoice, \"no_payment_method\")` before returning. That sends these customers through the same path as an expired card: the attempt count goes up, a retry is scheduled, the event is emitted, and the subscription goes to `past_due`.\n\nThe existing 24 tests pass. I didn't add a test for the no-payment-method case, and I didn't run that path myself. I wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"payments.py\", \"function\": \"collect\"}`.",
